noVNC, websockify, TigerVNC (`X0tigervnc`), fonts, and other third-party
components retain their
own copyright and license terms. Transport in a Xenoteer repository or image
does not relicense those components.

Production images place exact evidence under /usr/share/doc/xenoteer, including the
Debian package/source manifest, first-party file manifest, final-file ownership
manifest, Cargo component manifest, immutable source lock, and this notice.
Repository source/SBOM scripts live under scripts/licenses. Risk-spike-specific
version, license, and source decisions live under container/spikes.

These manifests are provenance and license evidence. They are not, by
themselves, a complete corresponding-source fulfillment bundle for a public
binary release. Release automation must assemble and verify the source artifacts
